udicó 35 contratos menores de obras de más de 37.500 y hasta 40.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 8,6 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 4,1, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,5 a 6,5. En diciembre se adjudicó el 6 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 8 % de todos sus contratos de obras. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 23 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 39.696,32 euros, se adjudicó en octubre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos cerca del límite no implica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se relacionan con otros adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 35 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 8.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.5 to 6.5. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 39,696.32 euros, was awarded in October 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices may be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by the body or contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the awardee A's contracts for repeated purchases of similar services. Review contract [1] to see if the amount is consistent with market rates. Look at the dates to confirm if multiple contracts were awarded for the same need in a short period.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["7OmRUG%2BPz6B4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D","WLz2XzbPVa3N3k3tjedSGw%3D%3D","tk83dNtEqvB4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}